# Every production `?` on a band decision inside a loop body, counted per
# file (scripts/gates/escalation-question-marks.sh). A loop that returns
# its first undecided reading refuses where a later reading would answer
# definitely: that is `geom_brep::ladder::climb`'s job. A new site reds
# until it is registered here with why its `?` is not a search's kept
# reading; a count that falls reds until it is lowered.
#
# HAND-ROLLED: a search or an identity that returns an escalation ahead
# of a later reading that could answer. Each is listed, with its port, in
# work/onecopy/question-mark-ladders-the-gate-registered.md; lower the
# count here as each is ported.
#
# solid_contain: point_in_faces's six on-face reads (any face holding the
# point answers OnBoundary), hand-rolled; ray_crossings's denominator, a
# crossing count, which needs every face.
crates/topo/src/boolean/solid_contain.rs 7
# rim_wedge: departures's abut (either pair abutting answers) and rides
# (either end off the line answers "not"), hand-rolled; sort_params, a
# sort, needs every comparison; reach reads every arc's traversal.
crates/topo/src/boolean/rim_wedge.rs 4
# containment: certify_plane (any margin decided apart answers "off the
# plane"), hand-rolled; conic_crossings, a crossing count, needs both roots.
crates/topo/src/splitting/containment.rs 2
# sectors: the crescent search's two reads (a crescent found answers),
# hand-rolled.
crates/topo/src/boolean/sectors.rs 2
# join: conic_pairs's first cut (which gap is first decided apart answers),
# hand-rolled.
crates/topo/src/splitting/join.rs 1
# shell: the moved walls' overlap search (an overlap found answers),
# hand-rolled.
crates/topo/src/shell.rs 1
# surface_group: Rim::holds (any coaxial margin decided apart answers "no"),
# hand-rolled.
crates/topo/src/boolean/surface_group.rs 1
# reduce: the line-cone apex end search (an end at the apex answers),
# hand-rolled.
crates/topo/src/boolean/reduce.rs 1
# ring_path: the lead-point read (an arc that is not a point answers
# None), hand-rolled.
crates/topo/src/ring_path.rs 1
# offset_derive: nearest's comparison, an argmin whose in-band comparison
# leaves the minimum open unless a later candidate is decided nearer than
# both; listed with the hand-rolled sites for that argument.
crates/topo/src/offset_derive.rs 1
# loft stacking: rim_pinned (any pair decided apart answers "not pinned"),
# hand-rolled.
crates/sweep/src/loft/stacking.rs 1
#
# NOT A SEARCH: every element is needed, so the first refusal is as good
# as any, or the read is the premise every later one needs.
#
# replace_face: every move's apex nappe and window.
crates/topo/src/replace_face.rs 2
# ray_walk: ray_crossings, a crossing count over every vertex and edge.
crates/topo/src/ray_walk.rs 2
# insert: section_chords's germ order, a sort over every group.
crates/topo/src/splitting/insert.rs 1
# edge_join: joinable reads both surfaces' chart class.
crates/topo/src/boolean/edge_join.rs 1
# blend battery: consumption_sweep strips every face.
crates/sweep/src/blend/battery.rs 1
# ssi section: roots decides every cluster's crossing.
crates/geom-brep/src/ssi/section.rs 1
# ssi march: each step's transversality, the premise of the next step.
crates/geom-brep/src/ssi/march.rs 1
# ssi ends: hermite reads both end states' transversality.
crates/geom-brep/src/ssi/ends.rs 1
# quartic: both quadratic factors' splits; every root is needed.
crates/geom-brep/src/quartic.rs 1
# props curved: sphere_boundary decides every edge's rim.
crates/geom-brep/src/props/curved.rs 1
